> Try to get two Elbereths on the square before you are really safe.

Two Elbereths doesn't make you "really safe"[**]; the whole text
will be subject to the random erasure, so wiping two characters,
one in each E-word, will make it ineffective, whether you wrote
them with one or many commands, whether in one or many turns. But
there *is* a difference in burning vs. carving vs writing in the
dust. The number of erased characters depends on what you actually
do; if I read the code correct...

Normal erasure: 1-3 characters [*]
While moving: 1-5 characters
While digging or attacking: 3 characters
While kicking or throwing: 2 characters

And levitate over an E-word to prevent it from being wiped out!

[*] Whether it happens during your turn depends also on your
     dexterity, probability is 1 in 40+3*Dex.

[**] There is no such thing as "real safety" in Nethack. ;-)

